From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] user32: preserve translated external-shell control clipping

Purpose: let builtin owner-draw Button and Static controls render inside the
XP Start panel's WM_PRINT snapshot. The shell supplies a translated MM_TEXT
memory DC. set_control_clipping converted the already logical client rectangle
through DPtoLP a second time, subtracting the viewport offset and intersecting
the valid clip with an unrelated empty region. Real API traces show successful
DrawText calls with an empty clip despite valid text, font and rectangles.
For external-shell opt-in and MM_TEXT, intersect the logical client rectangle
directly. Keep the prior conversion for mapped modes and normal Wine sessions.
The public tests/print-window.c regression verifies owner-draw builtin controls
in a translated DC along with nesting, clipping and caller-state preservation.
This changes only Wine source; no Microsoft binary or resource is modified.

diff --git a/dlls/user32/uitools.c b/dlls/user32/uitools.c
index a8f3a0a..7b42f01 100644
--- a/dlls/user32/uitools.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/uitools.c
@@ -129,7 +129,12 @@ HRGN set_control_clipping( HDC hdc, const RECT *rect )
         DeleteObject( hrgn );
         hrgn = 0;
     }
-    DPtoLP( hdc, (POINT *)&rc, 2 );
+    /* WM_PRINT supplies logical client rectangles in a translated MM_TEXT DC.
+     * Converting their coordinates again subtracts the snapshot viewport and
+     * can intersect the control's clip with an unrelated, empty rectangle. */
+    if (GetMapMode( hdc ) != MM_TEXT ||
+        !GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL", NULL, 0 ))
+        DPtoLP( hdc, (POINT *)&rc, 2 );
     if (GetLayout( hdc ) & LAYOUT_RTL)  /* compensate for the shifting done by IntersectClipRect */
     {
         rc.left++;
